From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:06:26 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: remove the segment and DMA-port helpers left unused

What the last four changes removed took the last caller of six more
functions with it: the software allocator over the carved segment pools
and its free counterpart, the free-segment push, the port-enable wrapper,
the counter mode selector, and a queue-index lookup that was a stub
returning zero.

None of them is reachable from the manager's probe, from the network
device or from anything else that stays. Remove them and their
declarations.

This also makes the driver build clean under W=1: the counter mode
selector computed a bit position it never used, which is an error under
this configuration's warning set and was the one thing standing between
the directory and a warning-free build.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

